<!doctype html>
<html lang="en">
<head>
<meta charset="utf-8">
<meta name="viewport" content="width=device-width, initial-scale=1">
<title>Agentic commerce readiness: {{ main.domain }}</title>
<link rel="preconnect" href="https://fonts.googleapis.com">
<link rel="preconnect" href="https://fonts.gstatic.com" crossorigin>
<link href="https://fonts.googleapis.com/css2?family=Schibsted+Grotesk:wght@400;500;700;900&display=swap" rel="stylesheet">
<style>
:root {
  --paper: #F7F8F6; --surface: #FFFFFF; --ink: #1B2430; --muted: #5E6873; --rule: #D9DDE1;
  --rung: #23577A; --rung-soft: #DCE7EF;
  --pass: #2E7D5B; --partial: #A86A12; --fail: #B23A3A; --info: #5E6873;
  --font: "Schibsted Grotesk", "Helvetica Neue", Arial, system-ui, sans-serif;
  color-scheme: light;
}
@media (prefers-color-scheme: dark) {
  :root {
    --paper: #12171D; --surface: #1A2129; --ink: #E7EBEF; --muted: #9AA5B1; --rule: #2C3640;
    --rung: #6FA8D1; --rung-soft: #22313F;
    --pass: #5CBF8F; --partial: #E0A44A; --fail: #E57373; --info: #9AA5B1;
    color-scheme: dark;
  }
}
* { box-sizing: border-box; }
body { margin: 0; background: var(--paper); color: var(--ink); font: 400 16px/1.55 var(--font);
       font-variant-numeric: tabular-nums; -webkit-font-smoothing: antialiased; }
main { max-width: 900px; margin: 0 auto; padding: 56px 24px 96px; }
a { color: inherit; text-underline-offset: 3px; }
a:focus-visible, summary:focus-visible { outline: 2px solid var(--rung); outline-offset: 3px; }
h1 { font-size: clamp(2.2rem, 6vw, 3.6rem); line-height: 1.02; font-weight: 900; letter-spacing: -0.03em; margin: 0 0 12px; overflow-wrap: anywhere; }
h2 { font-size: 1.5rem; font-weight: 700; letter-spacing: -0.01em; margin: 64px 0 6px; }
h3 { font-size: 1.1rem; font-weight: 700; margin: 0; }
.lede { color: var(--muted); max-width: 62ch; margin: 0; }
.meta { color: var(--muted); font-size: .9rem; margin-top: 18px; }

/* The ladder: the one memorable element. Rungs climb left to right. */
.ladder { display: grid; grid-template-columns: repeat(5, 1fr); align-items: end; gap: 6px; margin: 44px 0 10px; }
.rung { position: relative; background: var(--rung-soft); border-radius: 4px 4px 0 0; padding: 10px 10px 12px;
        display: flex; flex-direction: column; justify-content: flex-end; min-height: 64px; }
.rung:nth-child(1) { height: 72px; } .rung:nth-child(2) { height: 112px; } .rung:nth-child(3) { height: 152px; }
.rung:nth-child(4) { height: 192px; } .rung:nth-child(5) { height: 232px; }
.rung.reached { background: var(--rung); color: var(--surface); }
@media (prefers-color-scheme: dark) { .rung.reached { color: #0E1318; } }
.rung .name { font-weight: 700; font-size: .95rem; line-height: 1.15; }
.rung .you { position: absolute; top: -34px; left: 0; right: 0; text-align: center; font-weight: 900; font-size: .85rem; color: var(--ink); }
.rung .you::after { content: ""; display: block; width: 2px; height: 10px; background: var(--ink); margin: 4px auto 0; }
.rung .others { font-size: .75rem; line-height: 1.3; margin-top: 6px; opacity: .85; overflow-wrap: anywhere; }
.verdict { font-size: 1.25rem; font-weight: 500; margin: 26px 0 4px; max-width: 60ch; }
.verdict strong { font-weight: 900; }
.reason { color: var(--muted); font-size: .95rem; max-width: 70ch; margin: 0; }

.score { display: flex; gap: 32px; flex-wrap: wrap; margin-top: 28px; padding-top: 20px; border-top: 1px solid var(--rule); }
.score .big { font-size: 2.6rem; font-weight: 900; letter-spacing: -0.02em; line-height: 1; }
.score .small { color: var(--muted); font-size: .85rem; }

ol.fixes { padding-left: 1.4em; margin: 16px 0 0; }
ol.fixes li { margin: 0 0 14px; padding-left: 4px; }
ol.fixes .what { font-weight: 700; display: block; }
ol.fixes .how { color: var(--muted); }

.layers { margin-top: 16px; }
.layer { background: var(--surface); border: 1px solid var(--rule); border-radius: 10px; padding: 22px 22px 8px; margin-bottom: 14px; }
.layer header { display: flex; justify-content: space-between; align-items: baseline; gap: 16px; }
.layer .q { color: var(--muted); font-size: .92rem; margin: 2px 0 12px; }
.layer .pct { font-size: 1.6rem; font-weight: 900; }
.bar { height: 6px; background: var(--rung-soft); border-radius: 3px; overflow: hidden; margin-bottom: 8px; }
.bar span { display: block; height: 100%; background: var(--rung); }
.finding { border-top: 1px solid var(--rule); padding: 12px 0; }
.finding summary { cursor: pointer; list-style: none; display: grid; grid-template-columns: 76px 1fr; gap: 12px; align-items: baseline; }
.finding summary::-webkit-details-marker { display: none; }
.status { font-size: .8rem; font-weight: 700; }
.status::before { content: ""; display: inline-block; width: 8px; height: 8px; border-radius: 50%; margin-right: 6px; background: currentColor; }
.s-pass { color: var(--pass); } .s-partial { color: var(--partial); } .s-fail { color: var(--fail); }
.s-info, .s-skip { color: var(--info); }
.s-skip::before { background: transparent; border: 1.5px solid currentColor; width: 5px; height: 5px; }
.finding .title { font-weight: 500; }
.finding .sum { color: var(--muted); font-size: .92rem; display: block; }
.finding .inferred { font-size: .78rem; color: var(--muted); border: 1px solid var(--rule); border-radius: 99px; padding: 0 7px; margin-left: 6px; white-space: nowrap; }
.detail { margin: 10px 0 4px 88px; font-size: .88rem; }
.detail .fix { margin: 0 0 8px; }
.detail ul { margin: 0; padding-left: 1.1em; color: var(--muted); overflow-wrap: anywhere; }
.detail table { border-collapse: collapse; margin-top: 8px; font-size: .82rem; }
.detail td, .detail th { padding: 3px 10px 3px 0; text-align: left; border-bottom: 1px solid var(--rule); }

.compare-wrap { overflow-x: auto; margin-top: 16px; }
table.compare { border-collapse: collapse; width: 100%; min-width: 520px; }
table.compare th, table.compare td { padding: 10px 12px 10px 0; text-align: left; border-bottom: 1px solid var(--rule); }
table.compare th { font-weight: 700; font-size: .9rem; }
table.compare td.num { font-weight: 700; }
table.compare tr.total td { font-weight: 900; border-bottom: 2px solid var(--ink); }

.method { margin-top: 64px; color: var(--muted); font-size: .88rem; max-width: 70ch; }
.method p { margin: 0 0 10px; }
@media (max-width: 640px) {
  main { padding-top: 36px; }
  .ladder { gap: 3px; } .rung { padding: 6px; } .rung .name { font-size: .72rem; }
  .rung:nth-child(1) { height: 56px; } .rung:nth-child(2) { height: 84px; } .rung:nth-child(3) { height: 112px; }
  .rung:nth-child(4) { height: 140px; } .rung:nth-child(5) { height: 168px; }
  .detail { margin-left: 0; }
}
@media print {
  body { background: #fff; } main { padding: 0; } .layer { break-inside: avoid; }
}
</style>
</head>
<body>
<main>
  <h1>{{ main.domain }}</h1>
  <p class="lede">How ready this store is for AI shopping agents: whether they can get in, understand the catalogue, talk to the store, and complete a purchase.</p>
  <p class="meta">Scanned {{ main.finished_at }} · {{ main.pages|length }} pages · UCP schemas up to {{ main.ucp_schema_version }}</p>

  <div class="ladder" role="img" aria-label="Maturity ladder: {{ main.domain }} is at {{ main.tier }}">
    {% for t in tiers %}
    <div class="rung {% if loop.index0 <= main.tier_index %}reached{% endif %}">
      {% if loop.index0 == main.tier_index %}<span class="you">{{ "This store" if competitors else "Here" }}</span>{% endif %}
      <span class="name">{{ t.name }}</span>
      {% set here = competitors|selectattr("tier_index", "equalto", loop.index0)|map(attribute="domain")|list %}
      {% if here %}<span class="others">{{ here|join(", ") }}</span>{% endif %}
    </div>
    {% endfor %}
  </div>
  <p class="verdict"><strong>{{ main.tier }}.</strong> {{ tiers[main.tier_index].meaning }}</p>
  <p class="reason">{{ main.tier_reason }}</p>

  <div class="score">
    <div><div class="big">{{ main.score|round|int }}</div><div class="small">Readiness score out of 100</div></div>
    {% for key, meta in layers.items() %}{% if key in main.layer_scores %}
    <div><div class="big" style="font-size:1.6rem">{{ main.layer_scores[key]|round|int }}</div><div class="small">{{ meta.name }}</div></div>
    {% endif %}{% endfor %}
  </div>

  {% if fixes %}
  <h2>Fix these first</h2>
  <p class="lede">Ordered by how much each one holds the score back.</p>
  <ol class="fixes">
    {% for f in fixes %}
    <li><span class="what">{{ f.title }}</span><span class="how">{{ f.fix }}</span></li>
    {% endfor %}
  </ol>
  {% endif %}

  {% if competitors %}
  <h2>Against the competition</h2>
  <div class="compare-wrap">
  <table class="compare">
    <thead><tr><th></th>{% for r in all_results %}<th>{{ r.domain }}</th>{% endfor %}</tr></thead>
    <tbody>
      <tr><td>Maturity</td>{% for r in all_results %}<td>{{ r.tier }}</td>{% endfor %}</tr>
      {% for key, meta in layers.items() %}
      <tr><td>{{ meta.name }}</td>{% for r in all_results %}<td class="num">{{ r.layer_scores[key]|round|int if key in r.layer_scores else "–" }}</td>{% endfor %}</tr>
      {% endfor %}
      <tr class="total"><td>Score</td>{% for r in all_results %}<td>{{ r.score|round|int }}</td>{% endfor %}</tr>
    </tbody>
  </table>
  </div>
  {% endif %}

  <h2>What we checked</h2>
  <p class="lede">Open any line to see the evidence.</p>
  <div class="layers">
    {% for key, meta in layers.items() %}
    {% set fs = main.findings|selectattr("layer", "equalto", key)|list %}
    {% if fs %}
    <section class="layer" aria-labelledby="l-{{ key }}">
      <header><h3 id="l-{{ key }}">{{ meta.name }}</h3>
        <span class="pct">{{ main.layer_scores[key]|round|int if key in main.layer_scores else "–" }}</span></header>
      <p class="q">{{ meta.question }}</p>
      <div class="bar"><span style="width: {{ main.layer_scores.get(key, 0)|round|int }}%"></span></div>
      {% for f in fs %}
      <details class="finding">
        <summary>
          <span class="status s-{{ f.status.value }}">{{ status_label[f.status.value] }}</span>
          <span><span class="title">{{ f.title }}</span>{% if f.confidence == "inferred" %}<span class="inferred">inferred</span>{% endif %}
          <span class="sum">{{ f.summary }}</span></span>
        </summary>
        <div class="detail">
          {% if f.fix and f.status.value in ("fail", "partial", "info") %}<p class="fix"><strong>What to do:</strong> {{ f.fix }}</p>{% endif %}
          {% if f.id == "robots_ai_agents" and f.data.rows %}
          <table><thead><tr><th>Agent</th><th>Role</th><th>Home</th><th>Product</th></tr></thead><tbody>
          {% for row in f.data.rows %}<tr><td>{{ row.agent }}</td><td>{{ row.role }}</td>
            <td>{{ "allowed" if row.home else "blocked" }}</td><td>{{ "–" if row.product is none else ("allowed" if row.product else "blocked") }}</td></tr>{% endfor %}
          </tbody></table>
          {% endif %}
          {% if f.data.note %}<p>{{ f.data.note }}</p>{% endif %}
          {% if f.evidence %}<ul>{% for e in f.evidence[:14] %}<li>{{ e }}</li>{% endfor %}</ul>{% endif %}
        </div>
      </details>
      {% endfor %}
    </section>
    {% endif %}
    {% endfor %}
  </div>

  <section class="method">
    <h2>How to read this</h2>
    <p>Tiers are gates, not score bands: a store reaches a tier only when it meets that tier and every tier below it. The score weights six areas: {% for key, meta in layers.items() %}{{ meta.name|lower }} {{ meta.weight }}%{{ ", " if not loop.last else "." }}{% endfor %}</p>
    <p>Lines marked “inferred” are strong signals rather than proof. Bot-protection results come from requests using AI agents' user-agent strings; real agents may be verified by IP address or signature and treated differently. ACP (ChatGPT checkout) integrations are private, so they can only be inferred from the outside.</p>
    <p>The journey probe adds one item to the cart and opens checkout, then stops. It never enters personal details, submits a form or pays.</p>
    {% if main.notes %}<p>Notes: {{ main.notes|join(" ") }}</p>{% endif %}
  </section>
</main>
<script>
  window.addEventListener("beforeprint", () => document.querySelectorAll("details").forEach(d => d.open = true));
</script>
</body>
</html>
